1. EXTENDED OPERATING PRINCIPLE AND TYRE CONFIGURATION\
SSOD (Synchronized Surface Operation Dynamics) is not merely a mechanical axle lift; it is an intelligent operational layer for the vehicle chassis that transforms a traditional passive axle structure into a dynamic kinetic energy bank. The fundamental concept is to eliminate all unnecessary mass inertia and transform the airborne axle into an active component that prepares for road contact well before physical movement occurs. This is achieved by integrating electric propulsion, ultra-fast energy storage, and predictive software architecture into one seamless entity that optimizes the vehicle's energy economy and stability in real-time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Dynamic e-Sync and Predictive Hydraulics:
\f0\b0 \
When the system receives a command to swap axles, it does not drop the Sigma Axle (Axle B) as a passive mass. ZF hub motors accelerate the airborne tyre to an angular velocity that exactly matches the road speed. The software calculates the 
\f1\b predictive impact point
\f0\b0 : since the mechanical response time (Delta-latency) of hydraulic cylinders is typically 450 ms, the system opens the valves and ramps the hydraulic pump PWM power to maximum during the acceleration phase. This ensures the tyre touches the asphalt with Zero-Slip, eliminating coupling shock and tyre wear.\

\f1\b KERS Recovery and Zero-Inertia:
\f0\b0 \
As the axle rises, it acts as a generator. The hub motors brake the rotating mass to zero, and the resulting kinetic energy is immediately stored in the supercapacitor. This eliminates the gyroscopic effect caused by a spinning airborne tyre, significantly improving vehicle stability and handling during cornering.\

\f1\b ASIL-D Watchdog and Fail-Safe:
\f0\b0 \
The system features a real-time 
\f1\b Watchdog Monitor
\f0\b0 . The Master-ECU sends and receives a "heartbeat" signal every 10 ms. If code execution freezes or the CAN bus is disrupted, the Watchdog cuts power and locks the system into a mechanical Safe State. The 42CrMo4 rocker arm ensures that even if hydraulics fail completely, one axle is physically forced down as the other rises \'96 the vehicle can never lose its driving traction.\

