4. MATHEMATICAL CORE (TEXT FORMAT FOR COPYING)\
Phi = ABS( (V_gps * K_abs) - (Omega_axleB * R_dynamic) )\
(Synchronization Index. Target Phi < 0.02 before full road contact.)\
R_dynamic = R_nominal * (1 - (Load_coeff * Pressure_psi))\
(Dynamic radius calculated based on tyre deflection.)\
T_regen = (0.5 * J * Omega^2) / Delta_t\
(KERS torque during braking. Delta_t is the braking duration.)\
t_start_hyd = t(Phi_target) - Delta_t_latency\
(Predictive hydraulic activation considering 450 ms mechanical Delta-delay.)\
PWM_pump = (V_drop * K_flow) + Base_load\
(Hydraulic pump PWM power, adjusting dynamically based on descent speed.)\
